1
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,537
‎I'll focus on hosing down their firewalls.

2
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:40,498
‎Leaving you to handle the boots.

3
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:42,584
‎Got it.

4
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,756
‎Appreciate you takin' this, Meshuga.

5
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:51,468
‎Most old buggers like us
‎flamed out a good while back.

6
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:54,387
‎It's just good to see ya back in the game.

7
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,529
‎Hey, D.

8
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:40,994
‎Whaddaya wanna do today?

9
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,377
‎Roman?

10
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,589
‎Uh... yes?

11
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,299
‎Are you Kyoko?

12
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:56,885
‎...Uh, yeah. I'm Kyoko.

13
00:02:57,468 --> 00:03:01,097
‎Come on, we should go.
‎Time isn't on our side.

14
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:11,858
‎D? Wake up, D.

15
00:03:12,483 --> 00:03:13,484
‎D?

16
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:14,736
‎D!

17
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:17,614
‎It's just you...

18
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:22,035
‎My name's Kyoko. Big fan of your work.

19
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:28,958
‎Roman's told me
‎you're having trouble sleeping.

20
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:35,089
‎That you struggle with nightmares.
‎Thought I could be of some help to you.

21
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:40,637
‎She really knows this stuff.
‎Just hear her out.

22
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:42,639
‎Don't need help.

23
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,016
‎You know where the door is.

24
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:48,394
‎I won't keep you very long,
‎all I'm asking for is a minute.

25
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:52,732
‎Yupi! Hey, Yupi!
‎Stop lettin' strangers in!

26
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:55,902
‎Yupi's outside. We passed her out front.

27
00:03:56,527 --> 00:04:00,281
‎Goddamn it... Just leave,
‎all right? Both of you.

28
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:02,367
‎-But...
‎-I said go!

29
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:08,998
‎Hey! Do you ever see someone
‎who shouldn't be there?

30
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:12,293
‎Or hear a girl's voice?
‎Like an echo inside your head?

31
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:15,171
‎-Wait, Kyoko!
‎-Is she here right now?!

32
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:18,299
‎Are you outta your mind?

33
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,552
‎Why's your face... so familiar?

34
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:25,306
‎From the list!
‎That's why you're compatible!

35
00:04:26,432 --> 00:04:27,642
‎What list?

36
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:30,728
‎Who the hell are you?

37
00:04:31,437 --> 00:04:32,981
‎Uh... I...

38
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:01,384
‎Fuck!

39
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:12,812
‎D!

40
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:25,533
‎Hey! Did you see a small woman?

41
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,828
‎A small woman! She ran this way!

42
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:32,332
‎I was just passin' through...
‎How about you chooms?

43
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:34,208
‎You hidin' her?

44
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:40,798
‎D!

45
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:47,722
‎Well, shit. Guess he didn't see her...

46
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:49,223
‎Did you?

47
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:52,518
‎You've gotta stop! Get outta here now!

48
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,568
‎Who was that bitch?

49
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:03,529
‎I dunno, honest! I only just met her!

50
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:07,158
‎Said she watches our videos.
‎Knows a lot about cyberware and stuff...

51
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,869
‎-Then why was she here?
‎-Because you've been acting insane!

52
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:14,040
‎I'm worried about you, D!

53
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,584
‎Haven't been yourself lately!

54
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:20,296
‎You just attacked a total stranger.

55
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:22,048
‎And Kyoko, too.

56
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:25,885
‎She said you might be
‎goin' cyberpsycho, so I thought...

57
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,554
‎Cyberpsychosis?

58
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:30,681
‎Is that why you brought her?

59
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:33,434
‎Wait!

60
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:36,562
‎She knew about the raid...

61
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,815
‎And about the Arasaka file
‎with my name on it.

62
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:40,691
‎She knows why I'm on it.

63
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,112
‎-Are you sure?
‎-Capri showed me all the dirt.

64
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,196
‎Capri did?

65
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:47,323
‎Still doesn't mean
‎you can just ‎kill‎ people.

66
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:51,577
‎Cut the shit! You dragged her here
‎without knowing anything about her!

67
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,748
‎She wants to take Capri.

68
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,041
‎I know she does.

69
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:00,962
‎Is she really that important?

70
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:03,089
‎The fuck am I gonna do without Capri?

71
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:08,094
‎Look at what you're doin' with her power!

72
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:10,221
‎-Getting revenge!
‎-You're wrong!

73
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:12,181
‎This is murder!

74
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:13,891
‎Murder is just murder, D!

75
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,811
‎I'm doing this for my family.

76
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:18,521
‎You wouldn't understand.

77
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:20,106
‎No, you're doing this for you!

78
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:22,733
‎You say it's for the dead,
‎but that's a lie!

79
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,487
‎A lie?

80
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:32,493
‎Like I said...
‎There's no way you'd understand.

81
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:34,912
‎You're not like me.

82
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:37,290
‎What do you mean?

83
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:38,875
‎They're still here, Roman.

84
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,461
‎They never leave. Never.

85
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:43,379
‎It can't be a lie!

86
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,131
‎D...

87
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:48,259
‎But I'd be a liar if I gave up now.

88
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:56,517
‎Get lost.

89
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,644
‎And don't find your way back.

90
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:14,035
‎D.

91
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:16,412
‎We got a bite!

92
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:28,090
‎Who did you say?

93
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:30,927
‎Claims to be a researcher at Arasaka.

94
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:33,888
‎She's asking whether the Capricorn project
‎is of interest to us.

95
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:36,057
‎What?

96
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,320
‎Mom?

97
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:51,948
‎How long you been here?

98
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:53,449
‎Not all that long.

99
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,742
‎Really?

100
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:56,327
‎You shoulda woke me up.

101
00:08:58,704 --> 00:08:59,705
‎What?

102
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:05,795
‎What is it?

103
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:06,879
‎Stay still for me.

104
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:14,720
‎What's wrong?

105
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:18,099
‎No matter what happens...

106
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,435
‎Your mama will always love you.

107
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,108
‎Mom...

108
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:31,529
‎I haven't given up yet.

109
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,031
‎Yeah.

110
00:09:57,888 --> 00:09:59,515
‎Let's get one thing straight.

111
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,059
‎I'm prepared
‎to tell you everything I know.

112
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:05,855
‎But only with your assurance
‎I leave here unharmed.

113
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,607
‎Seems fair.

114
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:09,025
‎Uh-huh.

115
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:12,653
‎A "research expedition"
‎was sent to your camp.

116
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,698
‎The R&D department sought
‎candidates for their research.

117
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:20,036
‎Provided they met the criteria.

118
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:23,080
‎Criteria?

119
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:28,336
‎High empathy, strong implant tolerance...
‎A few boxes they needed checked.

120
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,879
‎What kinda research?

121
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:32,048
‎Weapons development.

122
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:36,636
‎Their ideal candidates differed
‎from project to project.

123
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:40,890
‎And the labs lacked the means
‎to find them on their own.

124
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:44,602
‎Hence the need
‎for Counterintel to step in.

125
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:47,521
‎So you're sayin' someone
‎in D's clan matched the bill?

126
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:48,814
‎Your man himself.

127
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:50,775
‎Me?

128
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:55,071
‎That so-called "research expedition"
‎was an extraction to secure you.

129
00:10:55,821 --> 00:11:00,493
‎Wanting to keep our books clean, we hired
‎a fixer to arrange it. That was a mistake.

130
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:03,996
‎Of all mercs, they subcontracted
‎the work to Maelstrom.

131
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,540
‎Those chromecrunchers could botch a job

132
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:08,834
‎even if you handed it
‎to them gift-wrapped.

133
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:12,088
‎A minor scuffle snowballed
‎into a slaughter.

134
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:15,257
‎Didn't know until later
‎you weren't even there.

135
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,093
‎Hold on.

136
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:21,347
‎You're saying I lost everyone
‎because you were looking for me?

137
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:23,140
‎Not us.

138
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:26,143
‎The company. Don't get it twisted.

139
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:28,229
‎So who gave the order?

140
00:11:28,312 --> 00:11:31,148
‎-An exec named Tanaka.
‎-Then let's go kill that jerk!

141
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:34,527
‎Is it true? Kenzo, Renée...

142
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,028
‎-D?
‎-Everyone's dead...

143
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:38,364
‎-You're too late.
‎-Huh? Whaddaya mean?

144
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:41,742
‎-Tanaka's already dead. He was killed.
‎-It's all my fault?

145
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,077
‎Killed?

146
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:47,581
‎Abducted and tortured
‎by some mercs. Fried his brain.

147
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:51,001
‎Leader of their crew, Maine,
‎didn't survive the ordeal either.

148
00:11:52,461 --> 00:11:55,131
‎What? Everyone's already dead?

149
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:57,174
‎How totally convenient.

150
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:58,342
‎It's the truth.

151
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,303
‎Name David Martinez ring a bell?

152
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:02,847
‎Like, obviously...

153
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:06,517
‎Wait, wasn't Maine the guy that...

154
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:11,105
‎Yes. He was there, too,
‎when they killed Tanaka.

155
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:13,566
‎That may not have been a coincidence.

156
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:14,650
‎Whaddaya mean by that?

157
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:16,610
‎Martinez was on the same list.

158
00:12:17,361 --> 00:12:20,322
‎The stunt he pulled later
‎may be related somehow.

159
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,367
‎Punk brat nearly killed me too.

160
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:25,369
‎Thought that shitstorm
‎had finally died out.

161
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:28,539
‎Then you showed up hungry for blood.

162
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:31,417
‎What you did to Jake
‎had me on edge, I'll admit.

163
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:33,961
‎Ready to wash my hands of this.

164
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,672
‎-What about me?
‎-Hmm?

165
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:39,800
‎What am I supposed to do now?

166
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:41,427
‎Do about what?

167
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:44,221
‎They're all dead because of me.

168
00:12:45,222 --> 00:12:47,224
‎And the whole thing was my fault...

169
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,310
‎What do I do?

170
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:52,813
‎I don't know. But if they're dead,
‎that means... it's over.

171
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,940
‎You have your revenge.

172
00:12:56,066 --> 00:12:58,235
‎Now, I've told you all I can.

173
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:00,070
‎I trust you'll keep your word.

174
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,575
‎It's not over.

175
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:07,119
‎It's far from over.

176
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:11,081
‎What are you--

177
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:28,057
‎That's right, D!
‎Who cares who gave the orders?

178
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:31,852
‎They're all the same.
‎Burn Arasaka to the fucking ground!

179
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:47,034
‎-Do it!
‎-Finish 'em!

180
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:04,134
‎Burn, Night City, burn!

181
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,764
‎Fuckin' gonks!

182
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:10,140
‎The hell are you thinkin'?

183
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:14,395
‎-Fuck you, pigs!
‎-C'mon!

184
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:16,564
‎See you in hell!

185
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:24,321
‎Crank up the heat!

186
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:26,282
‎You crazy bastards...

187
00:15:03,527 --> 00:15:06,864
‎If that'll be all,
‎another matter requires my attention.

188
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,541
‎Meshuga. In position.

189
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,628
‎Yeah, read you on ping. All set on my end.

190
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:23,172
‎I'll open sesame the back door
‎when you give it a knock.

191
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:25,132
‎Gimme one sec.

192
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:28,594
‎Avida, I want you to stay here.

193
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:31,055
‎Why? I'm going with you.

194
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:33,807
‎It ain't smart. Too much can go wrong.

195
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:37,353
‎We're here to choose Talia's new body.
‎I have to be the one to see it and decide.

196
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:41,857
‎King, sorry to butt in.
‎Somethin' you might wanna hear...

197
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,150
‎We have a problem?

198
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,735
‎Opposite, actually.

199
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:47,655
‎Got word there's a riot headed
‎for City Center.

200
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:50,908
‎Corp security's being pulled to support.

201
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:53,661
‎I'd say odds are the lab's
‎gonna be pretty short-staffed.

202
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:54,745
‎That's confirmed?

203
00:15:54,828 --> 00:15:57,748
‎Blastin' all over the news, yeah.

204
00:15:57,831 --> 00:15:59,792
‎That, and a drizzle in the forecast.

205
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:01,794
‎What's goin' on?

206
00:16:04,588 --> 00:16:07,383
‎Fine. We go together.

207
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:09,718
‎Hey, Hank, when we make our exit,

208
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:12,012
‎-whip the van to the back door.
‎-You got it.

209
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:26,026
‎There he is. Now's our chance.

210
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:37,830
‎The riots that erupted
‎in Wellsprings earlier today

211
00:16:37,913 --> 00:16:40,332
‎have led to violent clashes with the NCPD...

212
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:50,801
‎David! David!

213
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:55,973
‎David! Stop!

214
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:58,809
‎You again? You're not wanted here.

215
00:16:58,892 --> 00:17:00,436
‎Fucking likewise!

216
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:11,447
‎The hell are you doing? You're not
‎seriously going up against Arasaka?

217
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:14,033
‎They'll kill you!

218
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,831
‎David!

219
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:30,674
‎Oh, my God, D!

220
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:33,844
‎Can you believe this?

221
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,097
‎They don't learn.

222
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,475
‎They keep flyin' in just to get shot down.

223
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,228
‎What does it matter?

224
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:57,201
‎Uh... D?

225
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:03,040
‎D!

226
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:06,293
‎Get away from him!

227
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:08,045
‎What is that?

228
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:12,841
‎Wake up, D!

229
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:15,552
‎D! C'mon!

230
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,819
‎Well, that doesn't look good.

231
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:56,802
‎Daddy...

232
00:19:09,982 --> 00:19:12,776
‎Who the hell do you think made that chip?

233
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:16,155
‎Of course I thought to design a failsafe.

234
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,301
‎Target secured.

235
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:41,180
‎See how easy it is when you trust me?

236
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,723
‎What about your end?

237
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:44,308
‎Excellent work.

238
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:46,185
‎I'll be wrapping up here shortly.

239
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:48,437
‎Y'know... and I mean this as a compliment...

240
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,898
‎You're as corpo trash as they come.

241
00:19:57,905 --> 00:20:00,949
‎Behind that door
‎is the access point to Soulkiller.

242
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:02,201
‎And security?

243
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:04,119
‎Taking longer than expected...

244
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:06,955
‎Meantime, you focus on findin' a body.

245
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,707
‎Pick one.

246
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:11,627
‎We don't have time to shop around.

247
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:12,711
‎I know.

248
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:22,221
‎None of these are Talia...

249
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:24,640
‎You still have to choose.

250
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:30,395
‎Seein' my baby tear herself apart,
‎piece by piece. I couldn't bear it.

251
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:33,232
‎Now she has to lose all that's left?

252
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:35,734
‎She won't be my little girl anymore.

253
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:38,070
‎Didn't think of that before we started?

254
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:40,864
‎This is how we keep her alive,
‎don't have another choice!

255
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:42,366
‎I know that.

256
00:20:42,449 --> 00:20:45,118
‎The Talia you know will still be in there.

257
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,829
‎Right now,
‎all that matters is she survives!

258
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,248
‎I said I know...

259
00:20:50,374 --> 00:20:51,458
‎Oi, King!

260
00:20:51,541 --> 00:20:53,627
‎-What now?
‎-We got a sitch.

261
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:56,505
‎Riot's over, mob's dispersin'.

262
00:20:56,588 --> 00:20:58,131
‎Better get a damn move on.

263
00:20:58,215 --> 00:20:59,216
‎Understood.

264
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:01,385
‎Avida, we're outta time.

265
00:21:01,468 --> 00:21:04,263
‎If you won't make a decision, then I will.

266
00:21:07,432 --> 00:21:08,642
‎I've made up my mind.

267
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,649
‎Agh! The hell?

268
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:16,900
‎What's wrong?

269
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:19,653
‎No way... Fuck, fuck, fuck--

270
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:21,780
‎Meshuga? Meshuga!

271
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:23,532
‎Shit!

272
00:21:23,615 --> 00:21:25,534
‎Now Soulkiller...

273
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:28,745
‎Somethin' wrong?

274
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:31,081
‎Let's just get the body outside.

275
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:46,388
‎Hey! Meshuga's burned!

276
00:21:47,222 --> 00:21:48,265
‎He'll be fine.

277
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:49,933
‎Like hell he will!

278
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,563
‎-Fuck. C'mon!
‎-Dumbass!

279
00:21:58,317 --> 00:21:59,735
‎Dammit!

280
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:03,280
‎How'd there get here so fast?

281
00:22:05,699 --> 00:22:08,994
‎Him? Didn't Avida cover her tracks?

282
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:26,386
‎Shit... Let's go.

283
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:27,888
‎Avida!

284
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:49,409
‎Should we pursue?

285
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:52,329
‎No need. I've broken the man.

286
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:54,414
‎He no longer poses a threat.

287
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:56,792
‎Yes.

288
00:22:57,709 --> 00:23:00,962
‎My apologies.
‎It took longer than expected.

289
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,464
‎I'm returning now.

290
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:13,850
‎Good news. Think we lost 'em.

291
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,563
‎You were hit?

292
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:25,821
‎Shit... Where?

293
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:27,072
‎Where were you hit?

294
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:29,491
‎I'm sorry.

295
00:23:33,411 --> 00:23:36,206
‎Trauma Team should be here any minute.
‎You'll be okay!

296
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,459
‎Weak...

297
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:46,424
‎Please, Talia...

298
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:49,302
‎I know.

299
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:54,928
‎Subtitle translation by:
‎CD PROJEKT RED & Megumi Hunter
